/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think we should be unilaterally suppressing a warning when only a single scenario is triggering it. I'd sooner recommend suppressing the warning within the macro itself:\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/core/typedefs.h b/core/typedefs.h\r\nindex 91f5fda2ec5..1195379fb33 100644\r\n--- a/core/typedefs.h\r\n+++ b/core/typedefs.h\r\n@@ -339,8 +339,10 @@ constexpr bool is_fully_defined_v = is_fully_defined<T>::value;\r\n /// This can be used to reduce include coupling and keep compile times low.\r\n /// The check must be made at the top of the corresponding .cpp file of a header.\r\n #define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_TYPE(m_keyword, m_type) \\\r\n+\tGODOT_GCC_WARNING_PUSH_AND_IGNORE(\"-Wsfinae-incomplete\") \\\r\n \tm_keyword m_type; \\\r\n-\tstatic_assert(!is_fully_defined_v<m_type>, #m_type \" was unexpectedly fully defined. Please check the include hierarchy of '\" __FILE__ \"' and remove includes that resolve the \" #m_keyword \".\");\r\n+\tstatic_assert(!is_fully_defined_v<m_type>, #m_type \" was unexpectedly fully defined. Please check the include hierarchy of '\" __FILE__ \"' and remove includes that resolve the \" #m_keyword \".\"); \\\r\n+\tGODOT_GCC_WARNING_POP\r\n #else\r\n #define STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_TYPE(m_keyword, m_type)\r\n #endif\r\n```\r\n(This is assuming that the warning is suppressable during SFINAE. If not, disregard)","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119445#pullrequestreview-4293022286","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119445","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119445#pullrequestreview-4293022286"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119445"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-14T20:00:38Z","commi